      "nautiloid_cephalopods_radiate_shells_b": "Nautiloid cephalopods radiate. Shells become straight (orthocones), curved, and coiled. Sizes range from cm to METERS. The largest Ordovician cephalopods (Cameroceras, Endoceras) reached 6+ m — they were the apex predators of their seas.",
