      "hyphen": "- (hyphen)",
      "i_brahim_m_teferrika_1670_1747_was_a_h": "İbrahim Müteferrika (~1670-1747) was a Hungarian-born Ottoman convert + scholar who finally won permission from Sultan Ahmed III in 1727 to open the first Turkish-language printing press. The fatwa permitting it was carefully narrow: he could print on history, geography, dictionaries, and sciences — but not religious texts. The press printed 17 titles before Müteferrika's death; output was modest. Print expansion really accelerated only in the 19th century.",
      "i_can_explain_why_this_typography_comb": "I can explain why this typography combination yields this legibility state.",
      "i_love_typography": "I Love Typography",
      "i_love_typography_online_type_design_p": "I Love Typography (online type design publication)",
      "i_m_stuck_show_open_questions": "🤔 I'm stuck — show open questions",
      "if_the_typefaces_look_similar_on_your_": "If the typefaces look similar on your screen, your system may not have all of them installed. The fallbacks try to keep the right family (serif/sans/blackletter), but the exact letterforms vary.",
      "if_you_had_to_pick_a_font_that_represe": "If you had to pick a font that represents you",
      "illuminated_manuscripts": "Illuminated manuscripts",
      "imperial_22_30": "Imperial (22×30\")",
      "important_caveat_print_made_revolution": "Important caveat: print made revolutions possible at scales not previously possible, but did not cause them. Underlying political grievances drove the revolutions. Without those grievances, even massive print infrastructure would have produced no revolution. With those grievances + without print, revolutions would have happened but looked very different — smaller, slower, more localized. Print is a powerful enabling technology + a poor explanation for political change on its own.",
      "imposition_puzzle_folio_4_pages": "📑 Imposition puzzle (folio, 4 pages)",
      "imprimerie_royale_later_imprimerie_nat": "Imprimerie Royale (later Imprimerie Nationale)",
